# pdf.js's worker is vendored, minified, and re-copied out of node_modules by
# scripts/sync-pdf-worker.mjs on every prebuild. That copy carries the LF
# endings pdfjs-dist ships with, while core.autocrlf=true on Windows expects
# CRLF in the working tree — so the file showed as modified after every build,
# with no content change, every time. Treating it as binary stops git
# converting or comparing its line endings at all, which is the right
# treatment for a generated third-party bundle nobody edits by hand.
public/pdf.worker.min.mjs -text
